  "hook_title": "What if the Sun *vanished*?",
  "hook_seconds": 2.6,
  "shot_seconds": 3.5,
  "audio": {
    "music_db": -27,
    "sfx_db": -19,
    "native_db": -25,
    "seed": 15646
  },
  "voice_url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3KiaiPFpiBgipyl9nPlZn5fUZ7G/hf_20261018_172652_6bb7a225-e8aa-445d-811e-9c6e60859aa5.mp3",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "text": "What if the Sun vanished right now? For eight minutes, you would not notice anything at all. Here is why.",
      "image_url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3KiaiPFpiBgipyl9nPlZn5fUZ7G/hf_20261018_172554_f5a8016a-4364-4541-8716-bf30edee61a9.png",
      "motion_url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3KiaiPFpiBgipyl9nPlZn5fUZ7G/hf_20261018_172827_69871243-0c21-456b-a6f0-825b3f087919.mp4"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sunlight takes about eight minutes and twenty seconds to reach Earth, so the light already on its way keeps arriving.",
      "image_url": null,
      "motion_url": "https://images-assets.nasa.gov/video/GSFC_20140404_SDO_m11517_Flare/GSFC_20140404_SDO_m11517_Flare~large.mp4",
      "footage": true,
      "clip_start": 18.0,
      "clip_fit": "blur"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gravity changes also travel at the speed of light, so Earth would keep circling an empty spot for those same minutes.",
      "image_url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3KiaiPFpiBgipyl9nPlZn5fUZ7G/hf_20261018_172554_e16c5782-eb2d-4fe8-92c5-41d69dc583d7.png",
      "motion_url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3KiaiPFpiBgipyl9nPlZn5fUZ7G/hf_20261018_172827_473ec210-decb-4983-bb34-626f99e7f7fb.mp4"
    },
    {
      "text": "Then the sky goes dark and Earth flies off in a straight line. Plants stop making food from sunlight almost immediately.",
      "image_url": null,
      "motion_url": "https://images-assets.nasa.gov/video/Earth%20Views%20from%20the%20International%20Space%20Station/Earth%20Views%20from%20the%20International%20Space%20Station~large.mp4",
      "footage": true,
      "clip_start": 30.0,
      "clip_fit": "blur"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oceans would hold heat for a while, but the cold would win. Follow for more what-ifs about space.",
      "image_url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3KiaiPFpiBgipyl9nPlZn5fUZ7G/hf_20261018_172554_1f43ca5a-2452-49b8-ad8f-0aacab38684b.png",
      "motion_url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3KiaiPFpiBgipyl9nPlZn5fUZ7G/hf_20261018_172827_549fa9da-b3c5-4526-9b93-25474c83bb3e.mp4"
    }
  ]
}
